Subject: [PATCH] fix(tests): await extra silent-resume scenario children
 [daveey]

Three silent-auto-resume scenarios dispatch an ordinary replacement child
but return without awaiting its completion. In particular, the scenario
immediately before test_a_stop_while_auto_resume_is_off_still_cancels_a_promised_child
leaves a writer alive across the per-test HERMES_HOME switch.

Original CI: run 43684534856, job 132722245220, head
abdfe3e49dfb4b0ca6aec1c9df7216f0e4a6ad98, PR branch wt/lg-stdin-failclosed.
The first file run failed supersede_for_session == 1 (actual 0), with a
zero-byte state.db quarantine, record_unit_child readonly-database error,
and the model receiving session_db=None. The isolated retry passed.
Async ledger opens resolve the current home, so an unfinished old unit can
write into a later fixture's new database. Await the replacement's queued
completion inside the scripted-model patch, before changing config or home.
The completion queue follows durable persistence; no production semantics
or cancellation/no-respawn/no-event assertions change.

Add a deterministic held-model regression for all three scenarios. It
prevents the extra model turn from finishing until the scenario awaits its
completion, and reaps the executor on both RED and GREEN. Before the fix,
all three return with an unawaited child; afterwards all three pass. This
proves the leaked-worker lifetime, not every internal SQLite interleaving
from the historical failure.

Verification: full silent-auto-resume file plus auto_resume, continue,
resumable and new lifetime suite: 55 passed across 5 files. Exact original
stop test also passed alone before the fix; affected source files are
unchanged between incident head and current main. scripts/check --base
origin/main: all 20 checks pass. No retries, sleeps or weakened assertions.

